request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (The request is purely a display-order change on the watchlist page. The watchlist component owns the rendered list through its `movies` signal, so sorting there (unwatched first, stable within groups) satisfies the request without altering the store's data/persistence contract or any other consumer.)
round 1: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (Round 1 is red for two independent reasons. (1) My own acceptance test failed with NG0201 because the watchlist template's RouterLink needs ActivatedRoute and my TestBed setup did not provide the router — that is my test's flaw, so I am replacing it with a version that provides `provideRouter([])`, plus an extra test pinning that toggling still flips the store flag and reorders the list. (2) Two of the watchlist owner's own toggle tests now fail with "expected false to be true": either the sorting change broke the click→toggle wiring, or those tests' assertions encode the old insertion order (expecting the just-watched movie to remain at movies()[0]), which this request supersedes. The watchlist owner must fix the wiring if broken, otherwise use the test change-request protocol; the unwatched-before-watched contract from round 1 stands unchanged.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3 failed: Model hit max_tokens

